---
description: Conventions for editing the NestJS API under apps/api
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# `apps/api` conventions

- Runtime is Bun. Install deps with `bun add <pkg>` inside `apps/api/`, never
  `npm install`. The lockfile is `bun.lock` at the repo root.
- Every controller route MUST carry `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation` (with a
  stable `operationId`), and an `@ApiOkResponse({ type: SomeDto })`. Both
  request bodies and responses need typed DTO classes with `@ApiProperty`
  decorators so they appear in `/api/docs-json`.
- Business logic lives in a `*.service.ts`, NOT in the controller. The
  controller delegates to the service. The MCP tool in
  `src/mcp/mcp.service.ts` ALSO delegates to the same service, so the HTTP
  surface and the agent surface stay in sync. Every new route ships with a
  matching MCP tool registered via `server.registerTool(...)`.
- Tests live next to the code: `*.spec.ts` for unit (under `src/`),
  `*.e2e-spec.ts` for end-to-end (under `test/`). Mock the `DATABASE`
  provider with `.overrideProvider('DATABASE').useValue(...)` for routes
  that don't touch auth. Tests that exercise Better Auth (sign-up,
  sign-in, session) need a real Postgres: set `TEST_DATABASE_URL` and the
  spec runs; leave it unset and the spec auto-skips.
- Shared bootstrap wiring (global prefix, shutdown hooks, Swagger,
  Inngest mount) lives in `src/bootstrap.ts` so `main.ts` and e2e tests
  can both call `configureApp(app)` and stay in sync. Body parsing is
  owned by `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth`'s `AuthModule` — do NOT call
  `app.useBodyParser('json')` from bootstrap or main.
- Inngest functions go in `src/inngest/functions/<name>.ts`, one file per
  function. Re-export them via `src/inngest/functions/index.ts` so
  `bootstrap.ts` sees a flat list.
- Drizzle schema lives in `src/db/schema/<domain>.ts`, one file per domain,
  re-exported from `schema/index.ts`. `schema/auth.ts` is generated by
  `bun run db:auth-generate` — never hand-edit it. New tables ship with a
  generated migration (`bun run db:generate`) committed to the repo. Pool
  tuning is env-controlled: `PG_POOL_MAX`, `PG_IDLE_TIMEOUT`,
  `PG_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`, `PG_PREPARE` — see `src/db/index.ts`.
- Auth routes (`/api/auth/*`) are served by `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth`
  with a global guard. Anonymous endpoints (`/api/health`, `/api/mcp`,
  Inngest's webhook) MUST be decorated with `@AllowAnonymous()` from
  `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth`. Authentication options live in
  `src/lib/auth.ts`; transactional email templates live in
  `src/lib/auth-emails.ts`. Better Auth's instance is built outside the
  Nest DI container, so it uses the plain factories in
  `src/email/email.factory.ts` and `src/http/http.factory.ts` — keep those
  factories in sync with the Nest providers in `*.module.ts`.
- Auth flows (sign-up, sign-in, password reset, OAuth callback) are NOT
  exposed as MCP tools. They are user-initiated and depend on session
  cookies, which MCP's stateless Streamable HTTP transport cannot carry.
  The "one service, two surfaces" rule applies to first-party domain
  features, not to Better Auth's surface.
- Do NOT add code comments that narrate what the code does. Comments are for
  non-obvious intent, trade-offs, or constraints.
